# mutgap3_res_texture_record_clamps: The texture dimension check accepts three textures, each listed in its own exec beside a probe buffer, and each exec completes: a 4x4 RGBA8 cube whose six faces of 0xa00 bytes fill 0x3c00 of its one-page (0x4000) allocation (the allocation check counts 6 slices a cube; 7 would not fit); an RGBA8 2x8 texture of four levels (2x8, 1x4, 1x2, 1x1), whose expected width is clamped to 1 after each halving, so levels 2 and 3 are compared with width 1; and a BC1 8x32 texture of six levels whose width reaches 1 at level 3 and stays 1 through level 5, the compressed path's clamp.
